# Week 1 — C++ Program Structure & First Programs

**CSCE 306 · Object-Oriented Software Development · Fall 2026**
Professor Faisal Abbas · North Central College
**Dates:** Mon 8/24 & Wed 8/26 · **Readings:** Gaddis Ch. 1–2

Program structure, `cout`/`cin`, variables and data types, arithmetic and casts, constants, and formatted output. Pairs with the Week 1 VS Code / Git / GitHub setup: Lab 1 is your first commit.

## Folder layout

```
week01-cpp-intro/
├── README.md
├── examples/          in-class demo programs (one concept per file)
└── lab/
    ├── starter/       what students start from (contains TODOs)
    └── solution/      completed reference solutions
```

## Building

Every `.cpp` file is a standalone program unless noted. Compile any one of them with:

```bash
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra <file>.cpp -o <name>
./<name>
```


Most lab files end with a small test driver that prints `PASS`/`FAIL` per check. In several starters the driver is commented out (`/* Uncomment when ready ... */`) so the starter compiles cleanly before the class exists — uncomment it once your code is in place.

## Examples

| File | Concept |
|------|---------|
| `01_hello_world.cpp` | Anatomy of a C++ program |
| `02_cout_and_escapes.cpp` | Output with cout and escape sequences |
| `03_variables_and_types.cpp` | Variables and fundamental data types |
| `04_sizeof_and_limits.cpp` | How big is each type? (sizeof and numeric_limits) |
| `05_cin_input.cpp` | Reading input with cin and getline |
| `06_arithmetic_and_casts.cpp` | Arithmetic, integer division, and static_cast |
| `07_constants_and_auto.cpp` | const, constexpr, and auto |
| `08_formatting_output.cpp` | Formatting output with <iomanip> |

